  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Designed in response to ships being built by Germany, the class would have rivaled Imperial Japanese and American planned battleships in size, though with less firepower.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The Soviets contemplated as many as fifteen of these ships, but eleven were never laid down, and according to the article, construction of the first four was plagued by difficulties.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Designated Project 23, the Sovetsky Soyuz-class battleships were a class begun by the Soviet Union in the late 1930s but never brought into service.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 53,573 people read the English Wikipedia article, about 271× the usual daily figure of 198.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Sovetsky_Soyuz-class_battleship:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:Sovetsky_Soyuz-class_battleship:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:31Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, Russian had the most readers, with 257.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Sovetsky_Soyuz-class_battleship:2026-11-02",
        "views:ru:Линейные_корабли_проекта_23:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
